From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Madej <l.madej@grinn-global.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bcmdhd: skip WoWL on suspend

On non-Android builds dhd_pm_callback() calls dhd_set_wowl_active(TRUE)
and msleep(1000) on PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE, and dhd_set_wowl_active(FALSE)
on PM_POST_SUSPEND. On this board WiFi is not associated with any AP at
suspend time, so wowl_activate always fails and clutters dmesg on every
suspend:

  dhd_set_wowl_active: force wowl suspend setting
  dhd_set_wowl_active wowl_activate failed -1

The 1 s msleep is paid either way.

Wake-on-WLAN is not a use case on this board (suspend is driven from
local input, RTC or GPIO, not from network packets). Remove the WoWL
calls in dhd_pm_callback() so it becomes a no-op for WoWL and only
handles the SDIO wl_wdwake release path added by the companion patch.

Historically this was done by masking DHD_WOWL_IN_SUSPEND_SDIO in the
Makefile (the guard used by v2.4.0). Upstream v2.5.0 renamed the guard
in the source to DHD_ANDROID_IMG_BUILD and flipped its polarity, so the
Makefile route no longer disables anything. The change is now applied
directly on dhd_linux.c and depends on the companion stop-watchdog
patch being applied first (context is post-companion).

Signed-off-by: Lukasz Madej <l.madej@grinn-global.com>
---
 drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/dhd_linux.c | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/dhd_linux.c b/drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/dhd_linux.c
--- a/drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/dhd_linux.c
+++ b/drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/dhd_linux.c
@@ -1109,10 +1109,6 @@ static int dhd_pm_callback(struct notifier_block *nfb, unsigned long action, void
 	switch (action) {
 	case PM_HIBERNATION_PREPARE:
 	case PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE:
-#ifndef DHD_ANDROID_IMG_BUILD
-	dhd_set_wowl_active(TRUE);
-	msleep(1000);
-#endif /* DHD_ANDROID_IMG_BUILD */
 #ifdef BCMSDIO
 		/* Release wl_wdwake before SDIO suspend so that
 		 * dhd_os_check_wakelock() does not abort with -EBUSY. */
@@ -1124,9 +1120,6 @@ static int dhd_pm_callback(struct notifier_block *nfb, unsigned long action, void

 	case PM_POST_HIBERNATION:
 	case PM_POST_SUSPEND:
-#ifndef DHD_ANDROID_IMG_BUILD
-	dhd_set_wowl_active(FALSE);
-#endif /* DHD_ANDROID_IMG_BUILD */
 #ifdef BCMSDIO
 		dhdinfo = container_of(nfb, dhd_info_t, pm_notifier);
 		dhd_os_wd_timer(&dhdinfo->pub, dhd_watchdog_ms);
--
2.43.0
